                <head>459. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>In conformity with U.N. General Assembly Resolution 1348 (XIII), the Ad Hoc
                    Committee on the Peaceful Uses of Outer Space met in New York May 6–June 25.
                    Although five designated members, Czechoslovakia, India, Poland, the Soviet
                    Union, and the United Arab Republic, declined to participate, the committee
                    established legal and technical committees of the whole to consider various
                    aspects of the use of outer space. The United States was represented by
                    Ambassador Lodge, Loftus Becker (Legal Committee), and Hugh L. Dryden (Technical
                    Committee). For text of the report of the committee to the 14th session of the
                    United Nations General Assembly, adopted June 25, see U.N. doc. A4141.</p>
            </div>
